WEBVTT

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.430
You're my angel, Richard.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.940
If...

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.900
If I stay with you, we won't
be able to remain friends.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.320
How shallow I am.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.740
The moment I realize I love him,
I desire his love in return.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.950
What's wrong?

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.870
You'll be cold on your own, Richard.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.750
York of the white rose.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.300
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.840
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.430
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.990
Henry seems to have fled
while on a pilgrimage.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.950
You've seen his face,
have you not, Mr. Catesby?

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.750
If we managed to capture him, then--

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:50.040
Saving His Grace takes priority!

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.290
Give the places we've
already checked another look.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.290
Yes, sir!

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.840
What's this?

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.270
It can't be.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:16.690
No, I'm sure of it. That man is...

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:17.650
Henry.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:18.780
Your Grace!

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:22.360
Catesby.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.410
Wait; he's not our enemy.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:31.040
I was too injured to move for a time,
and this man saved me.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.170
But that man is--

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:37.170
My friend.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.630
Catesby, wait a moment.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:48.430
He's an old acquaintance of mine.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:50.890
He came to take me away.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.270
No!

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:56.400
I told you that I would leave
as soon as I was well.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.900
There are things that I must do.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:04.410
Winning George to our cause
and annihilating Lancaster.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.700
And... And when you've done them?

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.160
Can we be together always then?

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.830
Once the war is over,
there will be no place for me.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.510
Let's promise to meet
again under that tree.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:23.090
I'll always be waiting for you here.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.390
Very well.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.850
You have my word.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:36.650
I'm certain it will all be over
by this time next year.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.820
Then we'll meet here in a year's time.

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.740
It's a promise, Richard.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:45.240
A promise.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:53.660
Your Grace, who was that man?

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:57.130
I don't know his past, although
he said he was a shepherd.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:04.170
Catesby, have you ever loved someone?

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:08.220
If your love could never be requited,

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:11.680
would you still want to be with them?

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.690
To stay beside them forever,
unable to tell them how you feel?

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.490
What should I do now?

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:30.700
In George's eyes, I'm a traitor. What hope
do I have in a straightforward talk?

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:41.750
I remember when Christmas was approaching.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:46.510
The time when I lost Father.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:51.350
George can't have forgotten either.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:58.440
What's this about?!

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.900
Duke George.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.110
Why, if it isn't Your Grace!

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:05.070
Please believe me! I really saw him!

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:07.240
He's merely a lying drunk, sir.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:10.570
Nonsense! I saw him with my own two eyes!

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.580
Saw who?

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.290
A ghost with long hair.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:22.750
He glides along the castle walls
like this, glowing the whole time.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:28.300
Huh? I could swear I see
him behind Your Grace.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:31.340
Here's sixpence. Now go home.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:38.310
Take care, sir.
Spirits are stronger this time of year.

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:45.570
If anything's haunting me, it's no ghost.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.400
It's...

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.900
What's the matter?

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:53.200
The banquet is about to start.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.780
Now for the best part!

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.790
Let's choose tonight's "king"!

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:00.460
If there's a bean in your cake,
you're king!

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.330
Who's the lucky winner?

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.710
Why, it's Lord Warwick!

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.880
The throne is yours, Your Majesty.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.470
I suppose I've no choice.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:13.260
That should have been my seat.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:17.310
Why is Warwick sitting on that throne?

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:22.730
No. Henry is king, and the Lancastrian
prince will succeed him.

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:24.480
Where did I go wrong?

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:28.610
Now, Your Majesty, I shall summon
the actors for the masque.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:33.370
I was meant to be the king's nearest
brother and his heir apparent.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:37.740
Your Grace, the attendees wish to
present you with this splendid wine.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:42.370
Bring me all you have; I'll drink all
the wine in the castle dry!

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:45.840
I am the lawful King of England!

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:50.670
Where is he? Where is my son?

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:52.840
Father!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:08:03.020
Father, I pledge my life to
the battle for your crown!

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.940
Will you join me, George?

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:08.150
I will! I swear it, Father!

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:13.860
Your Grace, a breath of fresh air
might do you good.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:16.410
Oh, yes.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.790
You've had a bit too much to drink.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:25.710
I guess I got in the way of your party.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:30.920
I can leave without Your Majesty's help.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:41.680
Did I... Did I make the wrong choice?

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.940
Even if I did, it's too late now.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.030
An actor from the masque?

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:53.780
George.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:57.910
My son.

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:02.160
George, where is my crown?

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:06.370
Will a son of York dye
the white rose with blood?

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:09.170
I-Impossible.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:11.800
No, it can't be you.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:15.090
George, sully not the spirit of York!

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:19.300
Do so, and you will
receive your just deserts!

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:23.390
Come. Place the crown in my hands.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:26.480
Stop, Father!

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:42.620
A virtuoso performance, Catesby.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:46.370
You were the spitting image of my father.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:50.460
Continue spreading rumors of the ghost.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:55.470
Give George a glimpse of our
father at every opportunity.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:56.880
Yes, sir!

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:02.310
The more pressure we apply,
the more effective that flag will prove.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:06.600
George is simple. This will move
him more than any argument.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:10.770
It means making my father's
ghost our tool,

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:13.980
but all of this is to avenge his death.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:17.700
You're determined to defeat Lancaster?
To defeat Henry?

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:21.160
Naturally. He murdered my father.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:24.040
I won't let him off with
the Tower next time.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:28.330
I swear that I'll slay him
on the battlefield.

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:29.790
My Lord!

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:33.500
I bring news!
Edward has set sail for England

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.880
with the support of Burgundy!

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.800
Just you wait, Warwick.

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:43.260
I'm going to rouse a tempest.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:49.890
It will rage until a golden
crown gleams upon my brow!

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:53.520
What is your command, My Lord?!

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:57.860
Do you honestly believe that the King
of France has taken no measures?

00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:59.780
Full speed ahead!

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:04.660
Sail for our England's sake, even if
the storm winds would deny us!

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:10.420
Your Majesty.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.670
I wondered where you'd gone.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:16.460
Please come inside. You'll take ill.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:20.720
I'll remain here. I will not go to war.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:23.050
That's for the best.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:28.770
We shall speedily apprehend the Yorkist
nobles and gather loyal forces to--

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:30.730
Don't kill them!

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.900
I've had my fill of war.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.570
Overawe them with a massive
army and drive them off.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:41.950
The war will end if we stamp out our foes.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:44.450
Now, gentlemen, take leave of His Majesty.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.870
Farewell, my sovereign.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.580
Farewell, Your Majesty.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.540
By Your Majesty's leave.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:56.500
Allow me to kiss Your Majesty's hand

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:58.710
as proof of my loyalty.

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:04.720
Virtuous George,

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.640
may God be with you.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:12.440
The war will end?

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:20.650
Even if the body withers, the soul--
the spirit of vengeance--will endure.

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:28.740
You know I'm not going to try anything.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:31.290
This is to fool my mother.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.420
I'm disappointed in you, Edward.

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:37.790
Mother! You see, um--

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:41.800
Even Henry did his duty as a man.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:43.880
Is your courage less than his?

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:45.890
O-Of course not!

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:48.640
No, it must be.

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:52.680
You're less of a man than Henry is.

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:56.520
You're wrong. That can't be true.

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:03.110
Then prove it to me here and now.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:05.070
In your mother's presence.

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:11.910
A king must perform before
far more subjects than this.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:16.880
If this is beyond you,
then you are unfit for the crown.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.630
You understand, don't you, Anne?

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.260
No matter how deeply you love Richard,

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:28.550
as long as you're a woman,
she'll never requite your feelings.

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:36.060
Don't you mind?

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:39.060
I'm your wife.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:47.110
Duke Richard will never smile on me again.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:51.740
Your wife has more resolve than you.
It's like looking at Henry and me.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:52.870
Silence!

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.410
I'm not like my father!

00:13:56.410 --> 00:14:00.130
And inferior to him?
I could never be that!

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:05.050
Watch, Mother! I'll prove that
I'm a man to be proud of!

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:13.310
Wait.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:19.480
I'll be your wife,
but promise me one thing.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:24.110
If you capture Duke Richard
in battle, don't kill him.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:27.860
That was already my intention.

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:39.540
We're having no difficulties
raising an army.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:43.630
Yes, my lord. And Queen
Margaret's fleet should soon arrive.

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:48.930
Once her reinforcements swell our ranks,

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:54.060
the sham army Edward borrowed from
foreign powers will be no match for us.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:56.140
My Lord, who shall
welcome Queen Margaret--

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:58.600
I've already sent someone.

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.440
The most trustworthy man I have.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:13.910
Well done, Richard. I must thank
God for our safe reunion.

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:18.620
Edward, are these all of our forces?

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:22.460
I doubt that this will be
enough to win in battle.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.590
That's why I sent you.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:28.800
Unless George returns to us...

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:33.600
...then this is where Edward must fall.

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:43.560
George.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:47.980
Traitor! Have you forgotten that
my sister is the true queen?!

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:50.490
How could you forsake your
own brother for Henry?!

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:51.950
Be silent, Anthony.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:56.620
Answer me, George. Who do you serve?

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:03.670
I serve the King of England.
Isn't that obvious?

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:09.300
George, I am bound for York
as merely the Duke of York.

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:12.970
I have no other motive. Let me pass.

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:14.760
That I cannot do.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:21.690
Brother, I came here to serve a king!

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.230
Not a duke!

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:30.240
The House of York is the house of our
father, who shed his blood for England.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:32.360
I cannot bring it to ruin.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:36.990
Edward, proclaim yourself king at once!

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:40.040
This time, I will be your subject!

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:43.370
George!

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.040
My brother!

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:49.590
You are ten times dearer to me
now than when we parted.

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:54.050
Dearer than when I harbored
not a drop of hatred for you.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.930
E-Edward.

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:01.060
Warwick and his allies are
raising troops everywhere.

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:05.480
We'll slip between them and
reach London before they do.

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:08.360
They've left Henry alone in the palace.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:11.230
Once we get inside, he's ours.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:12.400
Henry!

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:18.950
We're bound for London?

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:22.750
We plan to head south after
raising troops in York.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:27.710
More should flock to our banner
now that George has joined us.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:28.840
Your Grace.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:33.760
Please allow me to see to Henry.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:35.220
What do you mean?

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:36.430
If you were to--

00:17:36.430 --> 00:17:37.550
Mr. Catesby!

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:41.640
Lord Hastings summons you.

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:46.060
Return to your master.
Your mission with me is over.

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:50.860
With my own hands...

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:56.570
My name is Edward Plantagenet,
and I am the rightful King of England!

00:17:56.570 --> 00:18:00.580
--...I'll take vengeance on
Henry for Father's death!
--Now, onward, brave soldiers!

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:07.960
So, you came to see me.

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:14.460
Please tell me: have I been a bad king?

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:20.050
I never turned a deaf ear
to my people's pleas.

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:26.100
I never deprived them of their
wealth or made them suffer.

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:27.480
I...

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:30.940
I never wanted to be king.

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:36.650
Do you want to go outside?

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:40.240
Of course you do; it's a lovely day.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:44.700
Once it gets a little warmer,
so many flowers will bloom.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.500
Then summer will come.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:51.170
Trees will bear fruit and
their leaves will fall.

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:53.960
And then, I'll be able...

00:18:57.670 --> 00:18:59.510
I'll be able to see you again.

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:03.390
Henry!

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:04.680
Where are you?!

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:10.440
Richard?

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:12.900
Buckingham! Where is King Henry?!

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:14.690
How should I know?

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:18.450
Warwick had me locked up
until mere moments ago.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.160
Wait! Are you planning to kill Henry?!

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.910
Your Majesty!

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:34.840
Please flee! The Yorkists have
invaded to take you prisoner!

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:40.050
If I'm captured now,
I'll never see Richard again.

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:44.100
Hurry! The confusion will mask
your escape if you go now!

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:48.730
What of Henry?!

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:51.350
We've searched the house,
but he's not here.

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:53.440
Search all of London!

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:56.270
I'll reward whoever finds him!

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:59.860
It wouldn't be wise to kill Henry now.

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:03.620
Rash actions will cost you
your brother's trust.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:08.750
You speak like a loyal subject.

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:11.580
Look at that.

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:15.000
Edward.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.380
Elizabeth!

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:23.130
I'm so glad you're safe.

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:24.720
I'm sorry for my delay.

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.890
Edward, this is your son.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:32.310
O Lord!

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.900
Bless this boy!

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:40.940
His heir is born,
and his brother returned.

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:45.990
Even if Edward were to die now, the throne
would not be yours immediately.

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:49.040
When did I wish for the throne?

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.370
It's high time you were honest.

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:56.580
I refuse to believe that my words
have never once moved you.

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:04.800
I'll always be waiting for you here.

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:15.980
I'll annihilate Lancaster
and avenge my father.

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:18.730
Then, it will all be over.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:21.280
Once there are no more
battlefields, I'll be--

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:28.070
I thought you were like me--
smoldering with constrained ambition.

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:31.790
It appears I was mistaken.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:36.710
How did they avoid our notice?

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:42.630
We were supposed to have them
hemmed in. What is George doing?!

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:48.430
Well, no matter. Edward can
take London or kill Henry,

00:21:48.430 --> 00:21:52.390
but he can't change the fact
that our forces outnumber his.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:58.940
Edward, I promise that I'll
take your head myself!
